text:
i&#x27;m also using a &quot;type safe&quot; templating engine (for kotlin, as a gradle plugin) of my own design that goes the other way - instead of embedding a model class into the template, a template class is generated that takes all the values as parameters.<p>i.e. MyTemplate.tpl.html<p><pre><code>    {if $foo}hello world, {$myname}!{else}goodbye, world.{&#x2F;if}
</code></pre>
which creates a kotlin class that can be used like this:<p><pre><code>    MyTemplate(
      foo = true,
      myname = &quot;bar&quot;
    ).toString()
</code></pre>
the biggest upside for me is that this way there&#x27;s full, free IDE support, i don&#x27;t need to write extra view models if the mapping isn&#x27;t 1:1 and performance is pretty good because in the end there&#x27;s no runtime parsing&#x2F;compiling&#x2F;interpreting except for the baseline JDK stuff (though there are even faster engines).<p><a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;codeberg.org&#x2F;h34tnet&#x2F;tempolin" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;codeberg.org&#x2F;h34tnet&#x2F;tempolin</a><p>warning: so far i&#x27;m the only user though, so don&#x27;t use it in production. also, i&#x27;m working on some improvements right now which haven&#x27;t been pushed yet.
